gate: CLOSED
v:4 c:$ m:navitrack-config role:dev x:tauri
task: S20 T3 — iOS init, then ios:build
sprint: S20
dep: S20-T2-legal-bundle-identifier.pd
requires: [MOBILE_TAURI, BUN]
test_mandate: ../intel/TEST-COVERAGE-MANDATE.md
quality_mandate: ../intel/CODE-QUALITY-MANDATE.md
invariants: ../S20-INVARIANTS.md

context: |
  bun run ios:build dies in scripts/sync-ios-version.sh because
  src-tauri/gen/apple/NaviTrack_iOS/Info.plist does not exist.
  Xcode 26.2 and the iPhoneOS SDK are installed. gen/ is gitignored.
  Run bun run tauri ios init so that plist exists. Do not commit gen/.
  If init writes a different Info.plist path, point the sync script
  at the plist init created. Do not rename the product.
  Do not run ios:build:appstore. Do not upload. Do not run live radio.
  Then bun run ios:build. If a new host error appears after the
  sync script passes, stop and record it. Do not guess a second fix.
  Package manager: bun. No pnpm or npm lockfile.

out:
  - gitignored iOS project via tauri ios init
  - sync script only if its plist path does not match init
  - append to sprints/S20/RELEASE-COMPILE.md

cmd:
  - bun run test
  - bun run ios:build

done:
  - ios:build gets past sync-ios-version.sh and compiles on this Mac
  - gen/ is not committed
  - The note records that result
  - No store upload and no live radio
  - `bun run test` passes
